{
  "programId": "com.digitalarsenal.flows.terrain-ingest",
  "name": "Terrain Pyramid Ingest Flow",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "engineLinkage": "bridge",
  "description": "OFF-FLEET pyramid builder for the quantized-mesh terrain tileset. One timer tick is ONE GRANULE CELL of work. mark_query reads the durable resume mark through hostcap/flatsql-query; granule_plan resolves the next cell of a REGION-PRIORITY enumeration that is a pure function of the config, and emits EIGHT hostcap/http-request descriptors - the 2x2 granule neighbourhood in elevation and water-body form, all over responseWire raw-body-v1 because a granule is megabytes of binary the connector's JSON dialect would base64-expand by a third - plus ONE plan frame carrying every tile of that level whose SOUTH-WEST CORNER lies in the cell. terrain-source:tile decodes that granule set ONCE, windowed to the union extent under a 256 MiB in-guest budget, and emits one $DTT record per tile with the water mask classified on the level's global post lattice; all-ocean tiles are NOT stored (they are identical, there are millions, and the serving flow synthesizes an unstored address inside published availability as exactly that). ingest_meta authors the storage attribution the storage lane cannot invent - dataset, batch, epoch - reading the tile report's recordsOut to catch a batch that reports success and stores nothing, and the primary granule response's ETag; hostcap/storage-ingest appends the batch; publish_request advances the resume mark FROM THE VERIFIED STORE RESULT, never at dispatch, so a crash between fetch and store re-runs the cell instead of leaving an invisible hole. NO PUBSUB ANNOUNCE IN V1 (Themis: a tileset-epoch announcement would be a SIGNED record and that contract is not cut). publish_request's optional announce request output is deliberately left UNWIRED rather than pointed at a placeholder; the $DTT records reach the fleet through the existing dataset-publication lane. Levels shallower than 8 are not built here: a tile wider than a granule breaks the containment the 2x2 neighbourhood rests on, and those levels are built by DOWNSAMPLING deeper tiles over the record store. granule_plan refuses them by name. PLACEMENT: this flow runs OFF-FLEET on the build machine under Docker linux/amd64 WasmEdge, the same law binaries are built under - never on host-01 or host-02, whose workload placement is the owner's.",
